@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# The registered external catalog families (gmeow:CatalogFamily) — the CLOSED set
# of external formalisms a logic:GroundingCorrespondence's logic:targetEndpoint may
# belong to, with each family's raise-only correspondence-count ratchet.
#
# The registry is DATA, read by the mappings stage (crates/pipeline) and by the
# shipped-bundle catalog gate (crates/pipeline/tests/correspondence_laws_bundle.rs).
# Neither carries a hardcoded family list: registering a catalog is an ontology
# edit, so the decision to admit a new external surface is reviewable content
# rather than a hidden Rust array. A target endpoint matching NO family, or
# matching MORE THAN ONE, is a hard failure at compile time.
#
# Adding a family is deliberate: mint the row with its stem(s), its authoring
# grounding slice(s), and the count the shipped catalog carries today. Lowering a
# gmeow:catalogTargetMinimum is forbidden — the floor rises with the catalog and a
# retired catalog loses its row outright.
#
# Ownership is the AUTHORING boundary (docs/GROUNDING.md, "External grounding
# ownership"): the grounding slice whose mappings/ directory holds the family's
# bridge cells. Most families have exactly one; the cross-cutting authorities
# (Wikidata at all three boundaries, RDFS and OBI at two) declare each home they
# are actually authored at rather than a convenient fiction.

# ── logic: — upper ontologies, logics, rule and validation dialects ───────────

gmeow:catalogFamily-gufo a gmeow:CatalogFamily ;
    rdfs:label "catalog family — gUFO"@x-gmeow-english ;
